-- ROOT-CAUSE-PROBE-AT-BIRTH-2 (2026-10-26, charter pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000419 ROOT-CAUSE-PROBE-AT-BIRTH-1, its ten tickets 1000301-1000310 and their PROBE-NEEDED-1 twins 1000396, 1000401, 1000402, 1000407, 1000413, 1000414, 1000442).
-- WHAT WAS FOUND (read 2026-10-26 from live qnfo-audit, read-only):
--   1. The management-personas workflow (fleet_tasks id management-personas, step rc-file) files a "ROOT-CAUSE-1: <family> keeps recurring" ticket when a family was reopened five times in 7 days. ORPHAN-GUARD-BIRTH-1
--      gives every new issue a contract, and for these tickets it is the generic superseded one (module probe-template-v3-generic, action VACUOUS-PROBE-V3-1) that measures nothing. Ten tickets were open on it. The
--      workflow knows when a ticket is done (step rc-close closes it when v_root_cause_quiet lists it), but the contract never said so, so every ticket was an open issue with no live verification path: it counted in the
--      probe of issue 2954 (45 such issues, 10 of them these) and bred a PROBE-NEEDED-1 twin from qnfo-fleet-control REOPEN-LIVE-PATH-3 (seven twins open, 1000396 to 1000442).
--   2. The fleet's own probe author (rtAuthorLivePathProbe) tried these tickets and failed: remediation.probe-author-reject rows for 1000302 to 1000304 read "env.AI is not bound" (before 0.49.2) and for 1000305 to
--      1000307 "dry-run: no such column" (a model guessed column names). A deterministic probe is cheaper and right: the closing condition is known.
--   3. Circularity found while designing the probe, and the reason it does not read v_root_cause_quiet as the text of issue 1000419 proposed: the view refuses a ticket whose active contract reads fail. A probe that counted
--      the view's rows would read 0 while it fails, the failing verdict would keep the row out of the view, and the ticket could never close. The probe below reads the underlying facts instead: the ticket is older than 24
--      hours and no issue of its family (the same family function as the recur-snapshot step) was opened or reopened in the last 24 hours, read from issue_lifecycle and not from the hourly issue_recurrence_now snapshot
--      (which is empty for an instant between its recur-clear and recur-snapshot steps and stays empty if the snapshot step ever fails: a false pass for every ticket).
-- WHAT THIS FILE DOES:
--   a. ops_config root_cause_probe_sql holds the probe text ({ID} is the ticket id). It has no write keyword and no semicolon, and it does not contain the text the PROBE-NEEDED-1 twin looks for in a probe that reads the status
--      of its own issue, so the twins of these tickets read ok as soon as the tickets are probed.
--   b. The workflow gets one step, rc-probe, appended (json_insert at steps[#], the pattern of migrations -2 to -6): it sets the contract of every open ROOT-CAUSE-1 ticket that still stands on the generic superseded
--      contract (status superseded, action starting VACUOUS-PROBE-V3-1) to that probe, status active, d1-query, expected 1. A contract another doer wrote is left alone. It runs last on purpose: the executor aborts a
--      workflow at its first failing step, so a step in the middle that failed every hour would stop the 90 steps behind it, while a last step that fails stops nothing.
--   c. The same statement runs once here for the ten tickets that are open now (the workflow would do it at its next tick; this makes it deterministic).
--   d. The failure mode root-cause-ticket-without-probe and its detector fm-root-cause-ticket-without-probe (a ROOT-CAUSE-1 ticket older than 2 hours on a superseded contract), and the decision.
-- PREDICTION: after apply the probe of issue 1000419 reads 0 and closes it, the seven twins read ok and close, and each ticket closes when its family has been quiet for 24 hours (1000304, family
--   METRIC-REGISTRY-STALENESS-1, has had no event since 2026-10-25T09:00Z and is 10 hours old: due at about 2026-10-27T07:36Z). The nine families that still recur keep their probes failing, which is true:
--   remediation_latest_pass_pct_7d moves by about -0.6 point (1070 of 1348 subjects pass today, 1070 of 1358 with the ten) and nothing is closed that should stay open.
-- spof-review: none added. No DELETE or DROP runs in this file, so it names no BACKUP table beyond the two it creates for the Rollback.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- BACKUP: bak_20261026_rcp2_workflow
-- Rollback: UPDATE fleet_tasks SET definition = json_remove(definition, '$.steps[' || (SELECT j.key FROM json_each(fleet_tasks.definition, '$.steps') j WHERE json_extract(j.value, '$.name') = 'rc-probe') || ']'), version = version + 1, updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 'management-personas' AND instr(definition, '"rc-probe"') > 0; UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = (SELECT b.status FROM bak_20261026_rcp2_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), last_verdict = (SELECT b.last_verdict FROM bak_20261026_rcp2_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), verify_probe = (SELECT b.verify_probe FROM bak_20261026_rcp2_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), action = (SELECT b.action FROM bak_20261026_rcp2_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), precondition = (SELECT b.precondition FROM bak_20261026_rcp2_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), module = (SELECT b.module FROM bak_20261026_rcp2_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), attempts = 0 WHERE module = 'root-cause-probe-at-birth-1' AND class IN (SELECT class FROM bak_20261026_rcp2_contracts); DELETE FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = 'fm-root-cause-ticket-without-probe'; DELETE FROM failure_modes WHERE fm_key = 'root-cause-ticket-without-probe'; DELETE FROM ops_config WHERE key = 'root_cause_probe_sql';

-- 0. Backups for the Rollback: the workflow text as it is now, and the contracts of the ROOT-CAUSE-1 tickets that are open now.
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261026_rcp2_workflow AS SELECT id, definition, version FROM fleet_tasks WHERE id = 'management-personas';

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261026_rcp2_contracts AS SELECT class, issue_id, status, last_verdict, verify_probe, verify_transport, action, precondition, module, attempts, next_due_at FROM remediation_contracts WHERE issue_id IN (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE status = 'open' AND title LIKE 'ROOT-CAUSE-1: % keeps recurring');

-- 1. The probe text.
INSERT INTO ops_config (key, value, note) VALUES ('root_cause_probe_sql', 'SELECT ''1'' AS expected, CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM agent_issues a WHERE a.id = {ID} AND a.created_at < (CAST(strftime(''%s'', ''now'') AS INTEGER) - 86400) * 1000 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_lifecycle l JOIN agent_issues b ON b.id = l.issue_id WHERE l.event IN (''opened'', ''reopened'') AND l.ts >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-24 hours'') AND b.id <> a.id AND b.title NOT LIKE ''ROOT-CAUSE-1:%'' AND CASE WHEN b.title LIKE ''METRIC-TRIGGER-%'' THEN substr(b.title, 1, 14 + instr(substr(b.title, 16), ''-'')) ELSE substr(b.title, 1, MIN(CASE WHEN instr(b.title, '' '') > 0 THEN instr(b.title, '' '') ELSE 999 END, CASE WHEN instr(b.title, '':'') > 0 THEN instr(b.title, '':'') ELSE 999 END) - 1) END = substr(a.title, 15, instr(a.title, '' keeps recurring'') - 15))) AS TEXT) AS observed', 'ROOT-CAUSE-PROBE-AT-BIRTH-2: closing probe of a ROOT-CAUSE-1 ticket, {ID} is the ticket id, read by the rc-probe step of fleet_tasks management-personas. Expected 1: the ticket is older than 24 hours and its family had no opened or reopened issue for 24 hours.')
ON CONFLICT(key) DO UPDATE SET value = excluded.value, note = excluded.note, updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE ops_config.value IS NOT excluded.value;

-- 2. The workflow step, appended once (the instr guard makes a replay a no-op).
UPDATE fleet_tasks
SET definition = json_insert(definition, '$.steps[#]', json('{"type":"sql","name":"rc-probe","db":"AUDIT","sql":"UPDATE remediation_contracts SET verify_probe = replace((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''root_cause_probe_sql''), ''{ID}'', CAST(issue_id AS TEXT)), verify_transport = ''d1-query'', status = ''active'', last_verdict = NULL, attempts = 0, deferred_since = NULL, next_due_at = datetime(''now''), module = ''root-cause-probe-at-birth-1'', precondition = ''a ROOT-CAUSE-1 ticket is open and its issue family may still recur (ROOT-CAUSE-PROBE-AT-BIRTH-2)'', action = ''MEASURES the closing condition of this ticket: its issue family has had no opened or reopened issue for 24 hours and the ticket is older than 24 hours. The management-personas workflow closes the ticket on the same condition (step rc-close) and the autoclose path closes it on the first pass, and a recurrence keeps this probe failing. ROOT-CAUSE-PROBE-AT-BIRTH-2'' WHERE status = ''superseded'' AND instr(action, ''VACUOUS-PROBE-V3-1'') = 1 AND issue_id IN (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE status = ''open'' AND title LIKE ''ROOT-CAUSE-1: % keeps recurring'') AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''root_cause_probe_sql'')"}')),
    version = version + 1, updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')
WHERE id = 'management-personas' AND instr(definition, '"rc-probe"') = 0;

-- 3. The same statement for the tickets that are open now.
UPDATE remediation_contracts SET verify_probe = replace((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = 'root_cause_probe_sql'), '{ID}', CAST(issue_id AS TEXT)), verify_transport = 'd1-query', status = 'active', last_verdict = NULL, attempts = 0, deferred_since = NULL, next_due_at = datetime('now'), module = 'root-cause-probe-at-birth-1', precondition = 'a ROOT-CAUSE-1 ticket is open and its issue family may still recur (ROOT-CAUSE-PROBE-AT-BIRTH-2)', action = 'MEASURES the closing condition of this ticket: its issue family has had no opened or reopened issue for 24 hours and the ticket is older than 24 hours. The management-personas workflow closes the ticket on the same condition (step rc-close) and the autoclose path closes it on the first pass, and a recurrence keeps this probe failing. ROOT-CAUSE-PROBE-AT-BIRTH-2' WHERE status = 'superseded' AND instr(action, 'VACUOUS-PROBE-V3-1') = 1 AND issue_id IN (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE status = 'open' AND title LIKE 'ROOT-CAUSE-1: % keeps recurring') AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ops_config WHERE key = 'root_cause_probe_sql');

-- 4. The failure mode and its detector.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO failure_modes (fm_key, failure_mode, root_cause, remediation, detector, probe_class, first_seen, issue_id, trigger_condition, symptom, blast_radius)
VALUES ('root-cause-ticket-without-probe',
  'a ROOT-CAUSE-1 ticket stands on the generic superseded contract, so it has no live verification path and breeds a PROBE-NEEDED-1 twin',
  'the management-personas workflow files the ticket (step rc-file) and ORPHAN-GUARD-BIRTH-1 gives it the VACUOUS-PROBE-V3-1 contract, the workflow knew its closing condition (step rc-close, v_root_cause_quiet) but never wrote it into the contract. Ten tickets, seven twins and 10 of the 45 issues counted by the probe of issue 2954 came from this',
  'ROOT-CAUSE-PROBE-AT-BIRTH-2 (migrations/2026-10-26-root-cause-probe-at-birth-2.sql): the workflow step rc-probe sets the contract of every open ROOT-CAUSE-1 ticket on the generic contract to a probe on the real closing condition (ops_config root_cause_probe_sql), in the same hourly run that filed it, and the migration applies it to the ten open tickets',
  'the d1-query contract fm-root-cause-ticket-without-probe counts open ROOT-CAUSE-1 tickets older than 2 hours whose contract is superseded (expected 0)',
  'fm-root-cause-ticket-without-probe', '2026-10-26', 1000419,
  'the workflow files a ROOT-CAUSE-1 ticket and the rc-probe step does not run in the same tick or does not match the contract (the step is last in a 96 step workflow, so an earlier failing step skips it until the next successful run)',
  'an open ROOT-CAUSE-1 ticket with a contract in status superseded and the action VACUOUS-PROBE-V3-1, and a PROBE-NEEDED-1 ticket for it one to two hours later',
  'one critical ticket per recurring family has no way to close and one medium twin per ticket is filed, and the 45-issue count of the probe of issue 2954 rises by one per ticket');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO remediation_contracts (class, issue_id, precondition, action, verify_probe, verify_transport, max_attempts, escalate_to, expected_cadence_h, status, module, budget_ms, max_items, requires_container, next_due_at)
VALUES ('fm-root-cause-ticket-without-probe', NULL, 'ROOT-CAUSE-PROBE-AT-BIRTH-2', 'failure-mode detector',
  'SELECT ''0'' AS expected, CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM agent_issues a JOIN remediation_contracts c ON c.issue_id = a.id WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND a.title LIKE ''ROOT-CAUSE-1: % keeps recurring'' AND c.status = ''superseded'' AND a.created_at < (CAST(strftime(''%s'', ''now'') AS INTEGER) - 7200) * 1000) AS TEXT) AS observed',
  'd1-query', 3, 'qnfo-fleet-control', 1, 'active', 'failure-mode', 45000, 5, 0, datetime('now'));

-- 5. The decision (decision_log is append-only: one row, guarded so a replay adds none).
INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'rem-a2 (remediation session 2026-10-26)',
  'a ticket whose closing condition the filing loop already knows should carry that condition as its probe from birth, and a probe must not read the view that refuses a failing contract (circular) nor a snapshot table that can be empty (false pass)',
  'ROOT-CAUSE-PROBE-AT-BIRTH-2: ops_config root_cause_probe_sql, step rc-probe appended to fleet_tasks management-personas, the ten open ROOT-CAUSE-1 tickets (1000301-1000310) re-pointed from the superseded generic contract to that probe (active, d1-query, expected 1), failure mode root-cause-ticket-without-probe with detector fm-root-cause-ticket-without-probe',
  'read 2026-10-26 from live qnfo-audit: ten open ROOT-CAUSE-1 tickets, all contracts superseded VACUOUS-PROBE-V3-1, seven open PROBE-NEEDED-1 twins (1000396, 1000401, 1000402, 1000407, 1000413, 1000414, 1000442), the probe of issue 1000419 read 10, issue_recurrence_now lists nine of the ten families as recurring (opens or reopens in the last 24 hours) and METRIC-REGISTRY-STALENESS-1 as quiet, v_root_cause_quiet lists none, management-personas fleet_runs ok at 17:36Z, the step executor (fleet-exec executeTask) runs steps in order and stops at the first throw',
  'applied through the canonical path on merge: the workflow gets its 96th step, the ten tickets get active contracts that read 0 until their family is quiet for 24 hours, the probe of 1000419 passes and closes it, the seven twins read ok',
  'one ops_config row, one appended step (an hourly UPDATE of at most the open ROOT-CAUSE-1 tickets that stand on the generic contract), ten contract rows, one failure mode, one detector contract, two backup tables, no issue status, trigger, worker or secret is touched',
  'the Rollback header of migrations/2026-10-26-root-cause-probe-at-birth-2.sql removes the step by name, restores the ten contracts from bak_20261026_rcp2_contracts (only while their module is still ours) and removes the config row, the detector and the failure mode, and bak_20261026_rcp2_workflow keeps the whole workflow text as it was',
  'root-cause-ticket-born-with-probe',
  'within 120 minutes of apply: the probe of 1000419 reads 0 and the issue closes, the seven twins close, ten tickets stand on active contracts, and each ticket closes on its own once its family is quiet for 24 hours',
  NULL,
  'node:sqlite replay of the migration (migrations/root-cause-probe-at-birth-2.test.mjs), the step SQL extracted from the stored workflow text and run on fixtures, the twin probe text of qnfo-fleet-control rtLivePathProbe, apply_migrations.py --check'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM decision_log WHERE actor LIKE 'rem-a2%' AND instr(action, 'ROOT-CAUSE-PROBE-AT-BIRTH-2') > 0);
